  "deviations": [
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Client\\Destinations\\IPRange::contains",
      "php": "inet_pton() throws a ValueError for an address containing a NUL byte, so contains() (and PublicInternet::allows()) throws.",
      "reason": "IpRange::contains and Destinations::allows return a bool; an address with a NUL byte is not contained (false). A connected address never holds one, so the transport is unaffected. IpRange::new still raises the ValueError for a range with a NUL byte. Destinations::allows is called with the address a socket reached, which is always a valid address; a fallible signature would burden every policy for an input that cannot occur."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Client\\Tls",
      "php": "V1_0 and V1_1 let cURL negotiate TLS 1.0 and 1.1 when the server offers nothing newer.",
      "reason": "The transport (rustls) speaks TLS 1.2 and 1.3 only: V1_0 and V1_1 floors behave as V1_2. rustls does not implement TLS 1.0 or 1.1, which are deprecated (RFC 8996)."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Client\\Adapter\\Curl\\Client::sendRequest",
      "php": "cURL follows a redirect to ftp:// or ftps:// (its default redirect protocols), and honours native options passed to the constructor (CURLOPT_PROXY, the http_proxy environment, CURLOPT_* in general).",
      "reason": "Http speaks HTTP and HTTPS only: a redirect to another scheme fails with ProtocolException 'The redirect target URL could not be parsed: Unsupported URL scheme', as any scheme cURL does not know does; there are no native cURL options and no proxy support. The native options array is cURL's own configuration surface, not part of the library's Adapter interface; the transport-neutral settings are all covered."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Client\\Client::withCertificate",
      "php": "An encrypted client key is decrypted with the passphrase.",
      "reason": "The passphrase is kept but rustls reads unencrypted PKCS#8, PKCS#1 and SEC1 keys only: an encrypted key fails with TlsException. rustls has no key decryption; decrypting PEM keys would need OpenSSL."
    }
